<body><table class="page" id="page"><tr style="height:1px"><td><table class="header"><tr><td class="logocell"><a href="/" title="EasyChair home page"><img class="leftlogo" src="/images/logoEC_short.png"/></a></td><td class="rolecell">EasyChair Smart CFP</td><td style="width: 99%"></td><td class="helplink"><a class="toplinks" href="/docs/home" title="User guide">User guide</a></td></tr></table></td></tr><tr style="height:99%"><td class="menu_and_content"><div class="menu" id="menu0"><table cellpadding="0" cellspacing="0" class="menu" style="position:static; visibility:visible"><tr><td class="top" id="menu1" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu1','/cfp',{&quot;a&quot;:null})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu1')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu1')" title="Main page">Home</td><td class="top" id="menu2" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu2','/cfp/choose',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu2')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu2')" title="Create a new CFP">New CFP</td><td class="top" id="menu3" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu3','/cfp/all',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu3')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu3')" title="Manage my CFPs">My CFPs</td><td class="top" id="menu4" onclick="Menu.followLink2('menu4','/cfp/watchlist',{})" onmouseout="Menu.hide('menu4')" onmouseover="Menu.show('menu4')" title="My CFP watchlist">Watchlist</td></tr></table></div><div class="search_row" id="cfp:search:row"><form action="/cfp/search" id="search-form"><input id="search-input" name="query" placeholder="Search" type="text"/></form></div><div class="summary"><div class="pagetitle">CFP</div></div><div class="content" id="content"><div class="subcontent"><div id="cfp" style="clear:right"><table class="title_table"><tr><td class="single"><div id="cfptitle">Network Flows 2.0: 13th DIMACS Implementation Challenge: Network Flows 2.0</div><div id="cfpvenue">Lehigh University</div><div id="cfpdateplace">Bethlehem, PA, United States, January 28-29, 2027</div></td></tr></table><table class="date_table"><tr><td>Conference web page</td><td><a href="https://coral.ise.lehigh.edu/flow-challenge-2-0/" target="_blank">https://coral.ise.lehigh.edu/flow-challenge-2-0/</a></td></tr><tr><td>Submission link</td><td><a href="https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=networkflows20" target="_blank">https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=networkflows20</a></td></tr><tr><td>Abstract registration deadline</td><td>September 15, 2026</td></tr><tr><td>Submission deadline</td><td>September 15, 2026</td></tr></table><div class="topics">Topics: <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=9905" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_blue bg_gray1">network flows</span></a> <a href="/cfp/topic?tid=39341" onclick="return EC.linkClick(event)"><span class="tag fg_blue bg_fuchsia">algorithm engineering</span></a></div><h2>Conference website</h2><p>https://coral.ise.lehigh.edu/flow-challenge-2-0/</p><p>The website contains detailed information about the event..</p><h2>Network Flows 2.0 Challenge Details</h2><p>The First DIMACS Challenge, devoted to network flows, took place in 1990-1991. The Challenge was a big success and started the tradition of DIMACS Challenges. The First Challenge greatly reduced the gap between theory and practice and raised standards for experimental work in the area. During the decades since the Challenge, network flow algorithms evolved, and new applications of network flows emerged. Many original benchmark instances are too easy for the improved implementations. Theoretical progress has been especially impressive, leading to near-linear algorithms for the minimum-cost flow problem and its special cases. Once again, experimental work is falling behind. The need for updated benchmarks and new algorithm implementations motivates the Network Flows 2.0 Challenge.</p><h2>Submission Guidelines</h2><p>All papers must be original and not simultaneously submitted to another journal or conference. In your experiments, you can use any instances you find useful, but you must also include core instances for the corresponding problem. We expect that most submissions will go beyond the core instances.</p><ul><li><strong>Extended abstract format:</strong> The main body of the extended abstract is limited to 8 pages using 12 pt font. This limit will be strictly enforced. Not counted in the page limit are (i) references (ii) an appendix containing data tables and figures.</li><li><strong>Submit </strong>your extended abstract using <a href="https://easychair.org/conferences/?conf=networkflows20">EasyChair</a>.</li><li><strong>No double submissions:</strong> We are treating the workshop papers as conference publications. No double submissions are allowed for the papers to appear in the proceedings. As mentioned above, we may allow some work to be presented without appearing in the proceedings.</li></ul><h2>Workshop Information</h2><p>The Challenge Workshop will take place on January 28-29, 2026, at <a href="https://www2.lehigh.edu/about/bethlehem-lehigh-valley">Lehigh University</a> campus in Bethlehem, PA, USA. This is just after the <a href="https://www.siam.org/conferences-events/siam-conferences/alenex27/">2027 SODA and ALENEX conferences</a>. These conferences will be in Philadelphia, PA, about 70 miles from Bethlehem.</p><p><strong>Deadline:</strong> The deadline for submitting papers to the Challenge workshop will be around September 15, 2026, soon after ALENEX acceptance notification. We expect to make acceptance decisions by October 15, 2026. The final versions of the accepted papers will be due on December 15, 2026. This will give the authors time to address reviewer feedback.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>All questions about submissions should be emailed to <a href="mailto:flowchallenge20@googlegroups.com" style="-webkit-tap-highlight-color:transparent; -webkit-text-stroke-width:0px; background-color:#ffffff; color:#1a73e8; cursor:pointer; display:block; font:400 13px / 20px Roboto, RobotoDraft, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif; letter-spacing:normal; orphans:2; outline:none; overflow:hidden; text-align:start; text-decoration:underline; text-indent:0px; text-overflow:ellipsis; text-transform:none; white-space:nowrap; widows:2; word-spacing:0px" target="_blank">flowchallenge20@googlegroups.com</a></p></div></div></div></td></tr><tr><td class="footer">Copyright © 2002 – 2026 EasyChair</td></tr></table></body></html>
